FORMAT dicom

%header

# ── Mark as de-identified ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DICOM PS 3.15 Annex E requires this tag to be set to YES
ADD PatientIdentityRemoved YES

# ── Linkage UIDs — explicitly preserved for re-identification mapping ────────
KEEP StudyInstanceUID
KEEP SeriesInstanceUID
KEEP SOPInstanceUID

# ── Patient identity ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Values are computed in dicom.py variable builders and injected via var:
REPLACE PatientID var:anon_patient_id
REPLACE PatientName var:anon_patient_name
REPLACE PatientBirthDate var:anon_birth_date
REMOVE PatientAddress
REMOVE PatientMotherBirthName
REMOVE PatientTelephoneNumbers
REMOVE PatientInsurancePlanCodeSequence
REMOVE MilitaryRank
REMOVE BranchOfService
REMOVE PatientReligiousPreference
REMOVE MedicalRecordLocator
REMOVE ReferencedPatientPhotoSequence

# ── Study / accession ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
KEEP AccessionNumber # REPLACE AccessionNumber var:anon_accession_number # Use if there is a method for keeping salt confidential.
KEEP StudyID # REPLACE StudyID var:anon_study_id # Use if there is a method for keeping salt confidential.

# ── Dates — jitter by var:date_jitter days ───────────────────────────────────
# date_jitter is an integer (days) set via DEID_DATE_JITTER env var (default 0)
JITTER StudyDate var:date_jitter
JITTER SeriesDate var:date_jitter
JITTER AcquisitionDate var:date_jitter
JITTER ContentDate var:date_jitter
JITTER InstanceCreationDate var:date_jitter
# PatientBirthDate is handled by REPLACE above (year + 0101)
JITTER endswith:Date var:date_jitter

# ── Times — zero out (preserve relative ordering within a study) ──────────────
BLANK StudyTime
BLANK SeriesTime
BLANK AcquisitionTime
BLANK ContentTime

# ── Physician / operator / institution ───────────────────────────────────────
KEEP ReferringPhysicianName
REMOVE ReferringPhysicianAddress
REMOVE ReferringPhysicianTelephoneNumbers
REMOVE ReferringPhysicianIdentificationSequence
REMOVE PerformingPhysicianName
REMOVE PerformingPhysicianIdentificationSequence
REMOVE NameOfPhysiciansReadingStudy
REMOVE PhysiciansReadingStudyIdentificationSequence
REMOVE OperatorsName
REMOVE OperatorIdentificationSequence
REMOVE InstitutionName
REMOVE InstitutionAddress
REMOVE InstitutionalDepartmentName
REMOVE IssuerOfPatientID
REMOVE contains:PhysicianName

# ── Device / station ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
REMOVE StationName
REMOVE DeviceSerialNumber
REMOVE PlateID

# ── Request / order ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
REMOVE RequestingPhysician
REMOVE RequestingService
REMOVE RequestedProcedureDescription
REMOVE RequestedProcedureID
REMOVE RequestedProcedureComments
REMOVE ReasonForTheRequestedProcedure

# ── Protocol / description (may contain free text PHI) ───────────────────────
# Comment these out if your downstream analysis needs protocol descriptions.
BLANK ProtocolName
BLANK StudyDescription
BLANK SeriesDescription

# ── UIDs — strip all secondary UIDs except those required for DICOM validity ──
# SOPInstanceUID, StudyInstanceUID, SeriesInstanceUID are left intact so the
# DICOM hierarchy is preserved. Remove the BLANK lines below if you want to
# generate fresh UIDs instead (requires generating them in engine.py).
REMOVE RequestedSOPInstanceUID
REMOVE StorageMediaFileSetUID
REMOVE UID

# ── Sequences / curves / overlays ────────────────────────────────────────────
# These are handled by strip_sequences=True in the engine; recipe entries here
# are belt-and-suspenders for sequence tags that may appear as top-level tags.
REMOVE ReferencedStudySequence
REMOVE ReferencedPatientSequence
REMOVE OtherPatientIDs
REMOVE OtherPatientIDsSequence
REMOVE OtherPatientNames

# ── Comments ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PatientComments carries structured field mapping (Project/Subject/Session)
REPLACE PatientComments var:patient_comments
BLANK ImageComments
BLANK VisitComments
BLANK AdmissionID
BLANK AdmittingDiagnosesDescription